{"type":"message","id":"70fb5113","parentId":"f4ac44b3","timestamp":"2026-05-24T04:23:49.449Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is running inside a Docker container (no systemd, no sudo, no doas, no brew). They're the `node` user without root access. They can't use `apt-get` to install packages. \n\nLet me check if they have npm (since it's a Node.js image), or if there's a way to install packages via other means.\n\nActually, the user is asking how to install SSH and gh CLI. Since I'm in a container without root, I should explain the situation and give them the right approach for their setup. But let me first check if they have any package managers available.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_265be0a57d634da8a9ee0a52","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"echo \"=== Node ===\" && node --version && npm --version && echo \"=== PATH ===\" && echo $PATH && echo \"=== npx ===\" && which npx 2>/dev/null"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"echo \\\"=== Node ===\\\" && node --version && npm --version && echo \\\"=== PATH ===\\\" && echo $PATH && echo \\\"=== npx ===\\\" && which npx 2>/dev/null\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779596602563,"responseId":"45b5b845f0954b2fba5b60406cf49e15"}}
