{"type":"message","id":"f274e7e7","parentId":"6f9df403","timestamp":"2026-05-24T04:34:07.635Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to use their OpenClaw (running in a container) to automatically execute GitHub backup tasks. They need SSH (for Git operations) and gh CLI for GitHub interactions. Let me figure out the best approach since we're in a container without root.\n\nFor the scenario:\n1. SSH → needed for `git push` to GitHub (via SSH key auth)\n2. gh CLI → for GitHub API operations, creating repos, managing backups\n\nSince we're in a container without root, I need to either:\n- Use the elevated gateway execution (I have `host` parameter in exec)\n- Or download binaries to local user directory\n\nLet me check if I can use `exec` with `host=\"gateway\"` or elevated mode to install packages.\n\nActually, looking at the exec tool, I have `host` which can be \"sandbox\", \"gateway\", or \"node\". And `elevated` for elevated permissions. Let me try using elevated to install packages via apt.\n\nWait, the exec tool description says:\n- `host`: \"auto\" | \"sandbox\" | \"gateway\" | \"node\"\n- `elevated`: Run on the host with elevated permissions (if allowed)\n\nLet me try the elevated approach to install openssh-client and gh.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"明白，老大要直接用这个容器环境来自动备份到 GitHub。那 SSH 和 gh 都要装。试试走 gateway"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cb659680991649319ebe93eb","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"apt-get update -qq && apt-get install -y -qq openssh-client gh 2>&1 | tail -10","elevated":true,"timeout":90},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"apt-get update -qq && apt-get install -y -qq openssh-client gh 2>&1 | tail -10\", \"elevated\": true, \"timeout\": 90}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"