{"type":"message","id":"64308c11","parentId":"7b73db18","timestamp":"2026-05-24T04:37:35.431Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so:\n1. `gh` CLI is installed and working ✅\n2. SSH is tricky - the static builds don't work because they're musl-based and we're on glibc. Let me try a different approach.\n\nActually, the user is using this container environment to do GitHub backups. Git is already installed and works. For GitHub backups, the main things needed are:\n- `gh` CLI ✅ (installed)\n- Git ✅ (already installed)\n- SSH → not strictly needed if we use HTTPS + token authentication\n\nFor backups using gh CLI:\n- `gh repo clone / gh repo list` - works with PAT/gh auth\n- `git push` via HTTPS with token - works without SSH\n\nSo the real question is: what kind of backup are we doing?\n\nIf we need SSH, I could:\n1. Try to build/compile ssh from source (too heavy)\n2. Use SSH through node modules (npm install ssh2)\n3. Use HTTPS auth with token instead\n\nBut wait - the user asked \"现在如何装ssh\" - how to install SSH. Let me try another source for static SSH binary that's glibc compatible.\n\nLet me try downloading SSH from a different source. Or I could try extracting ssh from the Debian package without dpkg.\n\nActually, let me try `apt-get download` to download the deb and extract the binary.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"gh 已就绪。SSH 从 Debian 包提取\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2f6236dd6beb48599b7f025a","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp\n# 下载 deb 包手动提取\napt-get download openssh-client 2>&1\nls *.deb 2>/dev/null","timeout":30},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp\\n# 下载 deb 包手动提取\\napt-get download openssh-client 2>&1\\nls *.deb 2>/dev/null\", \"timeout\": 30}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":