{"type":"message","id":"83e8a65b","parentId":"3e740dd2","timestamp":"2026-05-24T04:38:59.678Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The file is 300 bytes, probably an HTML redirect page, not the actual deb. Let me try a different approach to get the SSH binary. \n\nActually, thinking about this differently - for GitHub backup tasks, the user only needs:\n1. `git` - which is already installed ✅\n2. `gh` CLI - which I just installed ✅\n\nSSH is typically needed for `git clone/push` via SSH protocol. But:\n- If the user uses HTTPS with token (Personal Access Token), SSH is not needed\n- `gh` CLI itself handles auth via OAuth or token\n- `git` can use HTTPS remote URLs with credential helper\n\nSo actually SSH might not be necessary at all! The user can do everything with `git` (HTTPS) + `gh` CLI.\n\nBut let me try one more time for SSH since the user explicitly asked. Let me find the correct URL for the deb.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_bc0d5fd110124fd38636cb16","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp\n# Find correct package URL\ncurl -sL \"http://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/o/openssh/\" | grep -oP 'openssh-client_[^\"]+_amd64.deb' | sort -V | tail -3","timeout":15},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp\\n# Find correct package URL\\ncurl -sL \\\"http://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/o/openssh/\\\" | grep -oP 'openssh-client_[^\\\"]+_amd64.deb' | sort -V | tail -3\", \"timeout\": 15}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779597504397,"responseId":"82dc474ff953459bb9996bf4e4bb6956"}}
