{"type":"message","id":"70086b42","parentId":"fcabadf2","timestamp":"2026-05-24T04:42:13.265Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good - curl is available with libssh2 support. The container has curl with libssh2 (which can do SFTP/SCP) and libcurl linked with libssh2. But more importantly, git can work over HTTPS.\n\nFor a GitHub backup task, we don't necessarily need SSH binary. Git can work over HTTPS with tokens. And gh CLI is already installed and working.\n\nLet me also try to get the deb package from the correct pool for bookworm (Debian 12), which uses openssh 9.2p1.\n\nActually, let me rethink. The key question is: what does the backup task actually need?\n\nFor GitHub backup:\n1. `gh CLI` ✅ - already installed at ~/.local/bin/gh\n2. SSH for git push via SSH keys - this is nice but git can push via HTTPS with a token\n3. Git itself - ✅ already installed\n\nSo realistically, they can:\n- Use `gh` for repo management and API operations\n- Use git over HTTPS (with token) for clone/push operations\n- If they really need SSH, we can try a different route\n\nLet me try to get the correct deb for bookworm (9.2p1).","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"curl 已带 `libssh2`，git 走 HTTPS 完全没问题。先确认下 `openssh-client` 的正确包名"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e4f9156d19a84f86b094af94","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /tmp\n# 用 curl 直接下载正确版本的 deb  \ncurl -sL \"http://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/o/openssh/openssh-client_9.2p1-2+deb12u5_amd64.deb\" -o o.deb && file o.deb && ls -lh o.deb\necho \"---\"\n# 或者从 bookworm-security pool\ncurl -sL \"http://security.debian.org/debian-security/pool/updates/main/o/openssh/openssh-client_9.2p1-2+deb12u5_amd64.deb\" -o o2.deb && file o2.deb && ls -lh o2.deb","timeout":20},"partialArgs":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp\\n# 用 curl 直接下载正确版本的 deb  \\ncurl -sL \\\"http://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/o/openssh/openssh-client_9.2p1-2+deb12u5_amd64.deb\\\" -o o.deb && file o.deb &&